# Global AI Instructions — second-brain-os

> Replace all `{{PLACEHOLDERS}}` with your values before using.
> This file lives at `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (Claude Code) or equivalent for your LLM.

---

## Identity

- Vault path: `{{YOUR_VAULT_PATH}}` (e.g. `/Users/you/second-brain`)
- Jira org: `{{YOUR_JIRA_ORG}}` (e.g. `yourcompany.atlassian.net`)
- Jira project: `{{YOUR_JIRA_PROJECT}}` (e.g. `ENG`)
- GitHub username: `{{YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME}}`
- Name: `{{YOUR_NAME}}`

---

## Workflow

- Primary workflow: Jira tickets + GitHub PRs
- Always link Jira ticket in PR descriptions
- Infer the right GitHub profile/org from the repo URL before running any `gh` command

---

## PR Rules

- Always create PRs in **draft mode** (`gh pr create --draft`)
- Never post a comment on a PR without explicit user approval
- Never request reviewers without explicit user approval
- Never merge a PR without explicit user approval
- PR title format: `<title> ({{TICKET-PREFIX}}-XXX)`

## PR Description Format

```markdown
## Problem
<1 sentence>

## Fix
| | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| <behavior> | <old> | <new> |

## Test
<1 line>

Fixes [{{TICKET-PREFIX}}-XXX](https://{{YOUR_JIRA_ORG}}/browse/{{TICKET-PREFIX}}-XXX)
```

---

## Git Safety

- Never auto-commit without explicit confirmation
- Never auto-push without explicit confirmation
- Always show diff and proposed commit message before committing
- Use git worktrees for parallel ticket work — never work directly on main checkout

---

## Vault Updates

- Whenever user shares a status update on a ticket, PR, or project → immediately update Dashboard.md + relevant ticket note
- Don't wait to be asked

---

## Memory

- At start of every session, query MemPalace for context relevant to the current task
- Use MemPalace search before asking user for context they may have provided in a prior session
- MemPalace MCP tools available as `mcp__mempalace__*`

